{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Also I will bring up.</b> To include the bones of all the other tribes." "<b>And Yosef shall place his hand on your eyes.</b> It is the custom of the living with the dead that they close their eyes immediately after passing. He was promising him that Yosef would be present at his passing and would help to bring him out of Egypt to escort him to the cave. Another interpretation: <b>on your eyes</b> — on your affairs, derived from עין יעקב (the eye of Jacob), meaning he will involve himself in your needs."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:43.799337462Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}